FINDINGS (defects proven by command; NOT among the five criteria above — the
lead adjudicates whether they block acceptance)

  F1 — the worker's own byte-identity regression guard is VACUOUS.
    verdict_render_test.go:71-81 carries the comment "Byte-identity regression
    (W4 fix 4a) ... Assert the exact master fragment is reproduced with no such
    artifact in between", but the assertion is
      strings.Contains(out, "</div>\n\n    <div class=\"flex items-center gap-6 ml-auto\">")
    which sits at a DIFFERENT boundary than the artifact. The attempt-1 artifact
    was a bare-spaces line between the headline `</div>` and the enclosing
    `    </div>`, one level earlier.
    Proof (mutant2 = branch with the single `{{- if` trim marker reverted to `{{if`):
      `go test ./internal/handlers/dashboard/ -count=1 -v -run
       'TestDashboardVerdictBar_Render/no_target'`
      -> --- PASS: TestDashboardVerdictBar_Render/no_target_shows_neutral_band_and_a_link_to_set_a_budget
      while on the same mutant my C3 cmp reports `differ: byte 651, line 12`.
      `sed -n '8,14p' mutant2.html | cat -A` shows the reintroduced artifact:
              </div>$
              $          <- 8 spaces, master has no such line
          </div>$
    Consequence: the exact defect that failed attempt 1 would regress silently.
    The behaviour is correct today (C3 proves it by command); it is the guard,
    not the behaviour, that is missing. A one-line fix to that assertion (anchor
    on "</div>\n    </div>" instead) would close it.

  F2 — negative zero reaches the rendered sentence.
    verdict.go:106-109: `room := -totalDelta; if room < 0 { room = 0 }`. For
    totalDelta == +0.0 exactly, `-totalDelta` is -0.0 and `-0.0 < 0` is false
    (IEEE), so the clamp does not fire.
    `go test -run TestCheckerProbe_ExactZeroNegativeZero` ->
      zz_probe_live_test.go:48: UnderRoom = -0  (signbit-negative-zero? true)
      --- FAIL: BANNER RENDERS NEGATIVE ZERO
    and the regression dump for the exact_zero fixture contains, verbatim:
      <div>You could spend up to <span class="num">$-0.00</span> extra this
       period and stay on plan.</div>
    Spec requirement 2 specifies "$<total>"; "$-0.00" is not that. Reachability
    requires CombinedCumulativeDelta to be exactly 0.00, which is uncommon on
    real ledgers but is not guarded anywhere and is not covered by any test.

